        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in the Linux kernel's NVMe over TCP (nvmet-tcp) implementation. A race condition exists between the handling of an Initialization Connection Request (ICReq) and the teardown of a queue. A remote attacker, by sending an ICReq and immediately closing the connection, could trigger a double free vulnerability. This could lead to a denial of service (DoS) due to memory corruption.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "kernel: nvmet-tcp: fix race between ICReq handling and queue teardown",
